# SABOTAGE: T129 (reveal-grant clock property, determinism round 2) — `Samen.Reveal.Grants
# .active?/3`'s deny-on-read comparison is loosened from `>` to `>=`, so a grant stays
# ACTIVE at the exact instant it expires. One second of a privileged reveal window that the
# row says is over: clause (c) ("it DENIES the moment `now() > expires_at`") no longer holds
# at the one clock position where `>` and `>=` disagree.
#
# This is the off-by-one no signed-offset generator reliably catches. The property used to
# generate an offset in -7200..7200 and BRANCH on its sign, so the `offset == 0` position was
# exercised only on the runs where StreamData happened to produce a 0 — a seed-dependent
# proof of the boundary, which is no proof at all. The boundary is now PINNED in its own
# deterministic test (-1s allow / 0s deny / +1s deny), which is what makes this patch
# reliably refutable.
#
# Flips the named boundary red on every seed. The two properties around it stay green under
# this patch — strictly-before is still allowed, and at-or-after only disagrees at 0, which
# the generators reach only by chance — so the red fails because the boundary moved, not
# because the query, the requestor binding or the fixture broke.
#
# One comparison operator. Touches reveal/grants.ex ALONE.
# APP: samen_core
# TEST_FILES: test/reveal_grant_property_test.exs
# MUST_FAIL: the expiry boundary itself, pinned: ALLOW at -1s, DENY at 0s and +1s
diff --git a/samen_core/lib/samen/reveal/grants.ex b/samen_core/lib/samen/reveal/grants.ex
--- a/samen_core/lib/samen/reveal/grants.ex
+++ b/samen_core/lib/samen/reveal/grants.ex
@@ -521,7 +521,7 @@ defmodule Samen.Reveal.Grants do
             # a self-approved grant can never authorize a reveal).
             g.granted_by != g.requestor_id and
             is_nil(g.revoked_at) and
-            g.expires_at > ^now,
+            g.expires_at >= ^now,
         select: g.id,
         limit: 1
       )
